  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Women&#x2019;s Resilience to Disasters Programme (Pacific) 2021-2026</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Partnership with UN Women, the Women&#x2019;s Resilience to Disasters  (WRD) Programme contributes to making the lives and livelihoods of women and girls more resilient to disasters and climate change. The WRD Programme targets four Pacific countries: Solomon Islands, Kiribati, Vanuatu, and Fiji in adopting gender-responsive decision-making and governance systems enabling targeted action with civil society organisations to provide ownership to communities. This is complemented by a Pacific regional and a global advocacy component through a community of practice, the fostering of partnerships, providing technical support, coordination and engagement of policy and system changes.</narrative>
  </description>
